  "scoreProvenance": [
    "The complete concerto archive is immutable; spring-score-1.mid and the spring2 source definitions select only movement 2. Its published MIDI contains 1042 sounding note attacks over 117 quarter-note units.",
    "Source staves are solo violin, violin I, violin II, viola, and the written organ/cello bass line. Figured-bass symbols are retained visually but no realised continuo pitches or inferred separate double-bass part are invented. The source maintainer explicitly uses Anonymous.",
    "The source cello/organ part explicitly reads Largo Tacet for all 39 bars and its MIDI track contains no notes; only the four sounding source string staves are included in this movement’s voice list and engraving.",
    "Verified derivative syntax repair in spring-lys/spring2a.ly: Migrate the first accompaniment’s removed revert-auto-beam-setting calls: removing the three off-beat eighth-note boundaries makes 32nd-type beams span each quarter (8+8+8 thirty-seconds). Preserve LilyPond 2.24’s other 3/4 exceptions. The source’s first explicitly beamed bar shows this same quarter grouping. Full published pitch/onset multiset equality remains required.",
    "Verified derivative syntax repair in spring-lys/spring2b.ly: Apply the identical source-specified quarter-note beaming migration to the second accompaniment, preserving the default 3/4 eighth/triplet exceptions and explicitly grouping 32nd-type beams as 8+8+8. Original bytes remain unchanged; no note or written duration is altered."
  ],
